# The container image is built FROM A RELEASE TARBALL (see packaging/Dockerfile),
# not from this source tree, and the ONLY thing any stage reads is
# `dist/*.tar.gz`. Everything else — .git, target/, proofs/, bench-infra/ —
# would cost minutes per build for files nothing opens.
#
# The narrowness is load-bearing, not tidiness. `release-smoke` runs a
# container as root in a work directory and the quickstart leaves hundreds of
# megabytes of instance state behind it, including a mode-0600 admin key owned
# by root. If any of that were re-included here, the very next `docker build`
# would fail on a permission-denied while packing the context, three steps
# away from the cause. `!dist/*.tar.gz` selects the artifacts and nothing else,
# whatever a smoke run leaves lying around.
*
!dist/*.tar.gz
